 "honest_read": [
  "Native-faithful and class-exact: 0 class mismatches in 6 exports; every native index is exact at its texel centre and edges between distinct tones are crisp.",
  "Isolated single texels (rivets, lamp dots, 1-texel lines) survive as rounded-square cores of their native index (254 / 58 / 953 texels on D57D51A6 / 0FD152CA / C7C81B36). At 16x they read as round dots, not crisp square studs.",
  "Grilles and slats (D57D51A6) become smooth rounded bars; they read well at in-game size (panel C) but are soft at 16x.",
  "Staircase diagonals (0FD152CA top right) stay rounded staircases; they are not rebuilt as straight edges.",
  "Dithered dark areas (C7C81B36 pipe panels, D57D51A6 dark red plating) become soft blotches of the native tones, not real paint wear.",
  "The armour material is Stage 1 navy_armour + gunmetal_worn luminance detail at low amplitude (logD p1..p99 about -0.11..+0.10). On very light flat areas (0FD152CA) it reads as blotchy, stained-paper mottle rather than painted metal. A few small dark diagonal scratch strokes from gunmetal_worn are visible on flat fillers in the runtime-1024 view (C7C81B36, 0FD152CA). These are the least convincing part.",
  "Not a realism rebuild: no per-unit cut, no bevel or panel geometry, no stage-specific armour material. It is a safe index-space base."
 ],
 "known_limits": [
  "All keys are predicted-static: none has been seen live. The review CLUT is the static CLUT that draws the most of the page (a 'likely' pairing), not a proven one, so the colours on the review sheets may be wrong for the real enemy. Import only after the stage-4 run confirms each key.",
  "One render per page (the review CLUT); the other static predicted keys are listed as renderable_later and render from the same master once captured; palette-hold keys (runtime-written or multi-candidate CLUT positions) wait for AQ-05 phase lists.",
  "Review panel C is a SIMULATION (bilinear from runtime-2048, no mips, 9 px per texel); no in-game capture exists.",
  "No GP0 polygons or draw UVs exist for stage 4, so units are not cut (the Stage 1 t7/w4 vector step). Per-unit work waits for AQ-03 draw UVs.",
  "Material relief comes from the review CLUT's luminance; for a CLUT with a different tone order the relief can invert in places (zero-mean per index keeps average colours).",
  "Supersedes the unfrozen s4-enemies-2-13-v1 scratch folder, which was built with the pre-final w7lib (no lost-texel cores) and never frozen."
 ],
 "integration_notes": {
  "install": "do not install before the stage-4 acquisition run; then install only keys listed key-confirmed by validate_predicted.py confirm",
  "runtime": "runtime-1024 (4 px/texel) is enough for small enemies; runtime-2048 provided",
  "alpha": "PNG alpha = exact PSX classes (categorical)",
  "index_path": "master/<TEX>-labels16.npz (labels, weights) + <TEX>-logD8-f16.npy render any CLUT with w7lib.render"
 },
